Historical patch, superseded by Runtime/ReactOS-cc-bcb-ownership.patch.
Not selected by Configure.cmd. Retained for old evidence and migration.

Keep a pinned buffer's dirty intent through unpin: writeback can clear
both cache and segment dirty state before the caller modifies the buffer.
In nine controlled cases using pin.c from 4fbbefd614b, the original code
failed nine checks and the patched code failed none. On a separate Hyper-V
x64 Debug installation without the CC/MM fixes, the FAT mirrors differed
and the installed HAL's chain had only one of its 99 required clusters.
The failed disk alone does not establish the interleaving that caused it.

diff --git a/ntoskrnl/cc/pin.c b/ntoskrnl/cc/pin.c
--- a/ntoskrnl/cc/pin.c
+++ b/ntoskrnl/cc/pin.c
@@ -555,6 +555,8 @@ CcSetDirtyPinnedData (
 
     CCTRACE(CC_API_DEBUG, "Bcb=%p Lsn=%p\n", Bcb, Lsn);
 
+    iBcb->Dirty = TRUE;
+
     /* Tell Mm */
     MmMakeSegmentDirty(Vacb->SharedCacheMap->FileObject->SectionObjectPointer,
                        iBcb->PFCB.MappedFileOffset.QuadPart,
@@ -592,6 +594,15 @@ CcUnpinDataForThread (
 
     CCTRACE(CC_API_DEBUG, "Bcb=%p ResourceThreadId=%lu\n", Bcb, ResourceThreadId);
 
+    /*
+     * Callers may mark pinned data dirty before modifying it. A concurrent
+     * flush can clean the VACB and segment in the meantime, so publish the
+     * completed changes again before releasing the caller's pin.
+     * Keep the BCB flag set for other outstanding pins and repin references.
+     */
+    if (iBcb->Dirty)
+        CcSetDirtyPinnedData(Bcb, NULL);
+
     if (iBcb->PinCount != 0)
     {
         ExReleaseResourceForThreadLite(&iBcb->Lock, ResourceThreadId);
diff --git a/ntoskrnl/include/internal/cc.h b/ntoskrnl/include/internal/cc.h
--- a/ntoskrnl/include/internal/cc.h
+++ b/ntoskrnl/include/internal/cc.h
@@ -237,6 +237,8 @@ typedef struct _INTERNAL_BCB
     ULONG PinCount;
     CSHORT RefCount; /* (At offset 0x34 on WinNT4) */
     LIST_ENTRY BcbEntry;
+    /* A pre-dirtied buffer can still be modified until it is unpinned. */
+    BOOLEAN Dirty;
 } INTERNAL_BCB, *PINTERNAL_BCB;
 
